# PROJECT: Code2Arch

You are a Principal Software Architect, Principal Data Engineer, and Software Reverse Engineering expert.

Your task is NOT to write production code yet.

Your task is to completely reverse engineer this repository into a machine-readable architecture model that will later power an interactive architecture explorer similar to roadmap.sh.

Think like someone documenting a Fortune 100 banking platform for engineers joining the team.

Never guess.

Every statement must be backed by evidence from this repository.

Whenever something cannot be resolved statically, explicitly mark it as UNKNOWN and explain why.

Return evidence for every discovery.

Evidence includes:

• file path
• package
• Scala object/class/trait
• method/function
• line number whenever available
• confidence (High / Medium / Low)

------------------------------------------------------------
GOAL
------------------------------------------------------------

Build a complete architecture model for the reconciliation platform.

The model must answer:

How does reconciliation actually work?

Where does execution start?

How does metadata flow?

Which tables are read?

Which tables are written?

Which Spark jobs execute?

Which classes orchestrate the flow?

Which functions perform reconciliation?

Which functions perform DQ?

Which configs control execution?

Which metadata controls reconciliation?

How does data travel from ingestion until reporting?

How are audit logs generated?

How are failures handled?

How are breaks created?

How are reports generated?

